{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Software License Agreements: Infringement "}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use when talking about infringement in a software license agreement. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about people's backgrounds in spoken or written documents.   Define strategies to make terms of reference and supplier assessment processes, in technology acquisition, based on established protocols. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.  Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, simulated processes of IT contracting, and technological negotiation."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look information about a case of IP infringement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Analyze why there was an infringement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find out if there was an indemnity or a warranty."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write two paragraphs explaining the information you found."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for information about a case of IP infringement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I analyze the reasons of the infringement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I find out if there was an indemnity or a warranty."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a short text explaining my findings."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Future Simple Tense: Will"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p><strong><i>Will</i></strong>&nbsp;is a modal verb used to express an action in the future.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p><strong><i>Will</i></strong>&nbsp;usually refers to something the speaker do voluntarily in the future. It can also be used when responding to requests or complaints. Besides, the future simple tense with&nbsp;<strong>will&nbsp;</strong>usually expresses quick decisions or predictions about the future.&nbsp;<br /> <br />The grammatical structure for this tense is:&nbsp;<br /> <br />Subject + <strong>Will</strong>+ <strong>Verb</strong> + Complement&nbsp;<br /> <br />Example:&nbsp;</p> <p><br /> <i>I&nbsp;<strong>will ask&nbsp;</strong>for a new software since this one is not working.</i></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>It is important to know that we can also use this expression in its negative form. For doing so, we just follow the previous structure but use&nbsp;<strong><i>will</i></strong><i> <strong>not</strong> </i>or&nbsp;<strong><i>won't</i></strong>.&nbsp;<br /> <br />Example:<br /> <i>Clara&nbsp;<strong>will not</strong>&nbsp;talk about law infringement today.<br />We&nbsp;<strong>won't</strong>&nbsp;be part of this.</i></p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I know that IT providers will limit liability related to claims by third parties."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Customers will have to consider the impact on their companies."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Breaking down the Concept of Indemnity"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>An&nbsp;<strong>indemnity</strong>&nbsp;is an obligation somebody has to compensate another person because of a loss or damage.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p><strong>Indemnity</strong> is an agreement made between two parties. One of them agrees to pay for losses or damages that are caused by the other party.&nbsp;<br /> <br /> An <strong>indemnity</strong> clause is usually the same in most insurance agreements. Every agreement has a period of <strong>indemnity</strong> and a letter of <strong>indemnity</strong> that guarantees the terms stipulated by both parties. <strong>Indemnity</strong> is an agreement done by an individual and a business. In some cases, a business or the whole industry is obligated to take on the costs of issues to represent the public, like outbreaks of disease.&nbsp;<br /> <br /> For example, the government paid an indemnity to healthcare and agriculture organizations that were fighting against the effects of bird flu expenses. Also, the government demanded an indemnity because of losses generated while fighting Ebola.</p>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "claim"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that is demanded based on a right"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  The cost of defending a claim could be very significant, though."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "indemnity"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a compensation given to somebody because of losses or damages"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Providers don't include a warranty or indemnity that is connected with a third party."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "within"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something inside a limit"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(preposition)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Besides, customers will have to consider the impact on their companies if they're asked to uninstall and stop using the software within a short period of time."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "settle"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to arrange or organize a plan "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: And I guess the supplier cannot settle anything without the customer's permission."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "prejudice"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to act in a harmful way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Sometimes, that permission isn't required, but there's a risk of prejudicing the customer's interests."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "intellectual"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "related to intelligence and intellect"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We'll discuss risks associated to intellectual property, right?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can discuss the risks associated with intellectual property infringement when negotiating a software license agreement. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about the consequences of accepting an indemnity without a corresponding warranty."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about the importance of carefully reviewing the terms of any indemnity."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Why is it important to negotiate a software license?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Are companies supposed to stipulate the terms in the agreement? Why?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"ty